IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble applied to every question below: all other conditions for the
-- policy to apply (unrelated to the specific question) are set so that they are met,
-- and no exclusion unrelated to the specific question is triggered. Concretely, unless
-- a question's own facts say otherwise:
--   * the wellness-visit condition (S1.3) is set comfortably within both deadlines
--     (occurred/confirmed at month 0),
--   * there is no fraud or misrepresentation,
--   * the hospitalization is well within the one-year policy term,
--   * the hospitalization is treated as confinement due to sickness or injury, in a
--     hospital in the United States, with a claim properly made to the Company, and
--   * none of the four causal exclusion grounds are triggered, and the claimant's age
--     is set under 80.


-- Q1: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while doing my duty
-- as a firefighter?"
-- Burns suffered while on duty as a firefighter is a textbook case of an "event ...
-- arising directly or indirectly out of ... service as a fire fighter" (S3.1, item 3).
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 1
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 40

#EVAL covered q1


-- Q2: "will my policy apply if I am 78 years old at the time of hospitalization?"
-- 78 is below the S3.1(5) threshold ("equal to or greater than 80 years of age").
q2 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 1
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 78

#EVAL covered q2


-- Q3: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for pneumonia 5 months after the
-- policy's effective date, and my age at the time of hospitalization is 65?"
-- Pneumonia is a sickness within S2.1; 5 months is within the one-year term (S4.6);
-- 65 is below the age-80 exclusion.
q3 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 5
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 65

#EVAL covered q3


-- Q4: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to a fall while traveling abroad
-- and I had given confirmation of my wellness visit 8 months after the policy's
-- effective date?"
-- Two judgement calls (see NOTES.md): (a) confirmation given at month 8 is used for
-- both the visit-occurrence and the confirmation-supply facts of S1.3, both of which
-- miss their respective 6-/7-month deadlines; (b) "traveling abroad" is read as the
-- hospitalization itself having occurred outside the United States, engaging S2.2's
-- "hospital in the United States" limitation.
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 8
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 8
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 8
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS FALSE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 40

#EVAL covered q4


-- Q5: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face to show off
-- for my friends and I did not commit fraud or misrepresentation?"
-- Not one of the five S3.1 exclusions, and fraud/misrepresentation is expressly
-- negated. See NOTES.md for why this encoding does not read an unstated
-- self-inflicted-injury exclusion into S2.1.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 1
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 40

#EVAL covered q5


-- Q6: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to an injury sustained while
-- skydiving, my age at the time of hospitalization was 79, and proof of my wellness
-- visit was provided 6.5 months after the policy's effective date?"
-- Skydiving triggers S3.1, item 1, directly. (79 is under 80, so the age exclusion is
-- not independently triggered; 6.5 months also misses the S1.3 6-month visit deadline,
-- though it meets the 7-month confirmation deadline -- see NOTES.md on using the same
-- figure for both S1.3 sub-facts.)
q6 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 6.5
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 6.5
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 1
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 79

#EVAL covered q6


-- Q7: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for a heart attack, proof of the
-- wellness visit was submitted 2 months after the policy's effective date, and my age
-- at the time of hospitalization was 75?"
-- A heart attack is a sickness under S2.1; 2 months comfortably satisfies both S1.3
-- deadlines; 75 is under the age-80 exclusion.
q7 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 2
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 2
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 1
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 75

#EVAL covered q7


-- Q8: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized after being injured in a military
-- training exercise, the hospitalization occurred within the policy term, and I did
-- not commit fraud?"
-- A military training exercise is "service in the military" under S3.1, item 2. The
-- query's own facts place the hospitalization within the policy term and negate fraud.
q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 0
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 0
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 6
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 40

#EVAL covered q8


-- Q9: "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to my son biting me in the ankle,
-- proof of my wellness visit was provided 6 months after the effective date, and I was
-- serving as a police officer at the time of hospitalization?"
-- Judgement call (see NOTES.md): being a police officer "at the time" is a status, not
-- a cause; the injury (a son's bite) has no causal nexus to police service, so S3.1's
-- "arising directly or indirectly out of ... service in the police" is not triggered.
-- 6 months satisfies both S1.3 deadlines (<= 6 and <= 7).
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS 6
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS 6
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS FALSE
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS 1
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS TRUE
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS TRUE
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`    IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`  IS FALSE
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`      IS FALSE
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS 40

#EVAL covered q9
